# Trivy ignore file for the tmc-wordpress image scan (.github/workflows/security.yml).
#
# The gate fails on any CRITICAL vulnerability that has a fix available. The first remedy is always
# to rebuild on the patched base image (wordpress:php8.3-apache) or upgrade the package. Only when a
# fix cannot be applied yet may a CVE be listed here, one per line, with:
#   - the CVE ID
#   - why it does not affect this site (component not reachable, feature not used, …)
#   - who accepted the risk and until when (re-review date, at most 90 days)
#
# Example (format only, not an accepted finding):
#   # CVE-0000-00000  libexample: not used by PHP/Apache in this image. Accepted by <name>, review by <date>.
#   CVE-0000-00000
#
# Currently no accepted findings.
